/-!
# A perfect generator for `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)`

[Stacks, Tag 0A9A] (Rouquier, Theorem 6.8) reads, for `X` a quasi-compact and quasi-separated
scheme and `T ⊆ X` a closed subset whose complement is quasi-compact:

> the category `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` is generated by a single perfect object.

Here `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` is `Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported X T`, the objects of `D(𝒪_X)`
whose cohomology sheaves are quasi-coherent and supported on `T`, and "generated" is
[Stacks, Tag 09SJ]: an object `E` of the category with `Hom(P[n], E) = 0` for all `n` is zero.

The source runs the induction principle [Stacks, Tag 08DR], the inductive step extending perfect
objects with support by [Stacks, Tag 09IM]. The induction is carried out, with compact objects of
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` in place of perfect ones and Thomason's trick in place of Tag 09IM, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration/QcqsSupportedGeneration.lean`
(`Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.hasCompactSupportedGenerators`). What is added here is that
the generator produced there is perfect: a compact object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is perfect, which is
the implication "compact ⇒ perfect" of [Stacks, Tag 09M1].

## Main results

* `Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.isPerfect_of_isCompactObject_spec` — a compact object of
  `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` is perfect ([Stacks, Tag 06Z0] and [Stacks, Tag 07LT]).
* `Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.isPerfect_of_forall_derivedRestrict` — perfectness is local
  along a jointly surjective family of open immersions.
* `Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.isPerfect_of_isCompactObject` — a compact object of
  `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is perfect, for `X` quasi-compact and quasi-separated.
* `exists_isPerfect_quasiCoherentSupported_isWeakGenerator_of_qcqs` — **[Stacks, Tag 0A9A]**.

## Implementation notes

**The model.** Every statement is at the locally small model
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory`, the only one at which generation of
`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` is the statement consumed by Brown representability and by
[Stacks, Tag 0A9B]. The library's results on restricting perfect objects are stated at
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard`; they are moved to the locally small model through
complexes, perfectness of `Q(E)` being perfectness of the complex `E` at every model
(`Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.isPerfect_Q_obj_iff_isPerfectComplex`, [Stacks, Tag 08CN]).

**The generator** is a compact object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` as well; for the sibling
[Stacks, Tag 0A9B] it is available with that property from
`Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.hasCompactSupportedGenerators` together with
`Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.isPerfect_of_isCompactObject`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09M1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09M1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09SJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09SJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08CN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08CN)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for `R`-modules.
-- `D(R)` for sheaves of modules on a small site.
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] ModuleCat.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] SheafOfModules.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty
open CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated TopologicalSpace

universe u d

namespace Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration

open Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion Stacks.Duality.Supported

/-! ### Perfectness and the model of the derived category -/

section Model

/-- **A complex represents a perfect object exactly when it is a perfect complex**, at every
model of the derived category: one direction is [Stacks, Tag 08CN], the other the definition. -/
theorem isPerfect_Q_obj_iff_isPerfectComplex {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}}
    [HasDerivedCategory.{d} (StrictlyPerfect.OXMod.{u, u} X)]
    (E : CochainComplex (StrictlyPerfect.OXMod.{u, u} X) ℤ) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfect (DerivedCategory.Q.obj E) ↔ RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex E :=
  ⟨fun h => RingedSpace.isPerfectComplex_of_isPerfect_representation h ⟨Iso.refl _⟩,
    fun h => h.isPerfect⟩

section Standard

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- A complex restricted along `g` is perfect iff the restriction of its image in the standard
derived category is. -/
private theorem isPerfectComplex_restrictFunctor_iff_isPerfect_mapDerivedCategory
    {A B : Scheme.{u}} (g : A ⟶ B) [IsOpenImmersion g] (E : CochainComplex B.Modules ℤ) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex (X := A.toRingedSpace)
      (((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor g).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj E) ↔
    RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := A.toRingedSpace)
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor g).mapDerivedCategory.obj (DerivedCategory.Q.obj E)) :=
  ⟨fun h => Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_iso (X := A.toRingedSpace)
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor g).mapDerivedCategoryFactors.app E).symm
      (RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex.isPerfect.{u, u + 1} h),
    fun h => RingedSpace.isPerfectComplex_of_isPerfect_representation
      (Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_iso (X := A.toRingedSpace)
        ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor g).mapDerivedCategoryFactors.app E) h) ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩

/-- **Restriction along an isomorphism of schemes preserves perfect complexes.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isPerfect_restrictFunctor_mapDerivedCategory_of_isIso`, read at
the level of complexes, where it does not depend on a model of the derived category. -/
theorem isPerfectComplex_restrictFunctor_of_isIso {A B : Scheme.{u}} (g : A ⟶ B) [IsIso g]
    (E : CochainComplex B.Modules ℤ)
    (hE : RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex (X := B.toRingedSpace) E) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex (X := A.toRingedSpace)
      (((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor g).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj E) :=
  (isPerfectComplex_restrictFunctor_iff_isPerfect_mapDerivedCategory g E).2
    (Scheme.Modules.isPerfect_restrictFunctor_mapDerivedCategory_of_isIso g _
      (RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex.isPerfect.{u, u + 1} hE))

/-- **Perfectness of a complex is local on a scheme**: a complex whose restriction to a
neighbourhood of every point is a perfect complex is a perfect complex. This is
`Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_local_isPerfect`, read at the level of
complexes. -/
theorem isPerfectComplex_of_forall_restrict {X : Scheme.{u}} (E : CochainComplex X.Modules ℤ)
    (V : X → X.Opens) (hxV : ∀ x, x ∈ V x)
    (h : ∀ x, RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex (X := (V x).toScheme.toRingedSpace)
      (((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor (V x).ι).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj E)) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex (X := X.toRingedSpace) E := by
  have hK : RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := X.toRingedSpace) (DerivedCategory.Q.obj E) :=
    Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_local_isPerfect
      (X := X.toRingedSpace) (DerivedCategory.Q.obj E) fun x => ⟨V x, hxV x,
        Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_iso
          (X := (V x).toScheme.toRingedSpace)
          ((RingedSpace.derivedRestrictModulesIsoRestrictFunctor X (V x)).app _).symm
          ((isPerfectComplex_restrictFunctor_iff_isPerfect_mapDerivedCategory _ E).1 (h x))⟩
  exact RingedSpace.isPerfectComplex_of_isPerfect_representation hK ⟨Iso.refl _⟩

end Standard

/-- An object is perfect iff its chosen complex representative is a perfect complex. -/
private theorem isPerfect_iff_isPerfectComplex_objPreimage {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (K : DerivedCategory X.Modules) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := X.toRingedSpace) K ↔
      RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex (X := X.toRingedSpace) (DerivedCategory.Q.objPreimage K) :=
  ⟨fun h => (isPerfect_Q_obj_iff_isPerfectComplex _).1
      (Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_iso (X := X.toRingedSpace)
        (DerivedCategory.Q.objObjPreimageIso K).symm h),
    fun h => Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_iso (X := X.toRingedSpace)
      (DerivedCategory.Q.objObjPreimageIso K) ((isPerfect_Q_obj_iff_isPerfectComplex _).2 h)⟩

/-- The restriction of an object is perfect iff the restriction of its chosen complex
representative is a perfect complex. -/
private theorem isPerfect_derivedRestrict_iff_isPerfectComplex_objPreimage {A B : Scheme.{u}}
    (g : A ⟶ B) [IsOpenImmersion g] (K : DerivedCategory B.Modules) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := A.toRingedSpace) ((derivedRestrict g).obj K) ↔
      RingedSpace.IsPerfectComplex (X := A.toRingedSpace)
        (((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor g).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj
          (DerivedCategory.Q.objPreimage K)) :=
  let e := (((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor g).mapDerivedCategoryFactors).app
      (DerivedCategory.Q.objPreimage K)).symm ≪≫
    (derivedRestrict g).mapIso (DerivedCategory.Q.objObjPreimageIso K)
  ⟨fun h => (isPerfect_Q_obj_iff_isPerfectComplex _).1
      (Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_iso (X := A.toRingedSpace) e.symm h),
    fun h => Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_iso (X := A.toRingedSpace) e
      ((isPerfect_Q_obj_iff_isPerfectComplex _).2 h)⟩

/-- **Restriction along an isomorphism of schemes preserves perfect objects**, at the locally
small model of the derived category. -/
theorem isPerfect_derivedRestrict_of_isIso {A B : Scheme.{u}} (g : A ⟶ B) [IsIso g]
    (K : DerivedCategory B.Modules) (hK : RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := B.toRingedSpace) K) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := A.toRingedSpace) ((derivedRestrict g).obj K) :=
  (isPerfect_derivedRestrict_iff_isPerfectComplex_objPreimage g K).2
    (isPerfectComplex_restrictFunctor_of_isIso g _
      ((isPerfect_iff_isPerfectComplex_objPreimage K).1 hK))

/-- **Perfectness is local on a scheme**, at the locally small model of the derived category: an
object of `D(𝒪_X)` whose restrictions along a jointly surjective family of open immersions are
perfect is perfect. -/
theorem isPerfect_of_forall_derivedRestrict {X : Scheme.{u}} (K : DerivedCategory X.Modules)
    {I : Type*} {U : I → Scheme.{u}} (j : ∀ i, U i ⟶ X) [∀ i, IsOpenImmersion (j i)]
    (hcov : ∀ x : X, ∃ i y, j i y = x)
    (h : ∀ i, RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := (U i).toRingedSpace) ((derivedRestrict (j i)).obj K)) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := X.toRingedSpace) K := by
  choose i y hy using hcov
  refine (isPerfect_iff_isPerfectComplex_objPreimage K).2
    (isPerfectComplex_of_forall_restrict _ (fun x => (j (i x)).opensRange)
      (fun x => ⟨y x, hy x⟩) fun x => ?_)
  let φ := (j (i x)).isoOpensRange
  have hφ : φ.inv ≫ j (i x) = (j (i x)).opensRange.ι := by
    rw [Iso.inv_comp_eq]
    exact (Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange_hom_ι _).symm
  exact (isPerfectComplex_restrictFunctor_of_isIso φ.inv _
    ((isPerfect_derivedRestrict_iff_isPerfectComplex_objPreimage _ K).1 (h (i x)))).of_iso
    ((NatIso.mapHomologicalComplex
      (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorCongr hφ.symm ≪≫ Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorComp φ.inv _)
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).app _).symm

end Model

/-! ### Compact objects are perfect -/

/-- **A compact object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` is perfect**, at the locally small model. Under the
equivalence `D(R) ≌ D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0] it is a compact object of `D(R)`,
hence a bounded complex of finite projective modules ([Stacks, Tag 07LT]), whose associated
complex of sheaves is strictly perfect. -/
theorem isPerfect_of_isCompactObject_spec (R : CommRingCat.{u})
    (L : Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentDerivedCategory (Spec R)) (hL : IsCompactObject.{u} L) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := (Spec R).toRingedSpace) L.obj := by
  let M := (derivedTilde R).objPreimage L
  let eM : (derivedTilde R).obj M ≅ L := (derivedTilde R).objObjPreimageIso L
  have hM : IsCompactObject.{u} M :=
    (isCompactObject_iff_isCompactObject_obj (derivedTilde R) M).2 (isCompactObject_of_iso eM hL)
  obtain ⟨P, a, b, ha, hb, hfin, hproj, ⟨eP⟩⟩ :=
    (StacksDraft.Perfect.AnyModel.isPerfect_iff_isCompactObject_max.{u, u} M).2 hM
  have hbdd : {i : ℤ | ¬ IsZero (P.X i)}.Finite := by
    refine (Set.finite_Icc a b).subset fun i hi => ?_
    simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hi
    exact ⟨not_lt.1 fun h => hi (P.isZero_of_isStrictlyGE a i h),
      not_lt.1 fun h => hi (P.isZero_of_isStrictlyLE b i h)⟩
  have hsp := Stacks.AffineTilde.isStrictlyPerfect_tildeComplex_of_projective P hbdd
    fun i => ⟨hfin i, hproj i⟩
  let ι := (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec R).Modules)
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec R).ringCatSheaf)).ι
  exact Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexTriangles.isPerfect_of_iso (X := (Spec R).toRingedSpace)
    ((((tilde.functor R).mapDerivedCategoryFactors).app P).symm ≪≫
      (tilde.functor R).mapDerivedCategory.mapIso eP.symm ≪≫
      ((derivedTildeCompι R).app M).symm ≪≫ ι.mapIso eM)
    (RingedSpace.isPerfect_Q_obj_of_isStrictlyPerfect hsp)

/-- **A compact object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is perfect**, for `X` quasi-compact and quasi-separated,
at the locally small model: the implication "compact ⇒ perfect" of [Stacks, Tag 09M1]. Its
restriction to every affine open `Spec R ⟶ X` is compact, the direct image along the open
immersion commuting with direct sums ([Stacks, Tag 08DZ]), hence perfect
(`Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.isPerfect_of_isCompactObject_spec`), and perfectness is
local. -/
theorem isPerfect_of_isCompactObject (X : Scheme.{u}) [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (K : Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X) (hK : IsCompactObject.{u} K) :
    RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := X.toRingedSpace) K.obj := by
  have hV : ∀ x : X, ∃ V : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen V ∧ x ∈ V := fun x => by
    obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, -⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.1 X.isBasis_affineOpens)
      (Opens.mem_top x : x ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens))
    exact ⟨V, hV, hxV⟩
  choose V hVa hxV using hV
  refine isPerfect_of_forall_derivedRestrict K.obj (fun x => (hVa x).fromSpec) (fun x => ?_)
    fun x => ?_
  · obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : x ∈ Set.range (hVa x).fromSpec := by
      rw [(hVa x).range_fromSpec]
      exact hxV x
    exact ⟨x, y, hy⟩
  · let j := (hVa x).fromSpec
    have : ∀ α : Type u, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete α)
        (Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentDerivedPushforward j
          (Stacks.Duality.isQuasicoherent_homology_derivedPushforward_of_qcqs j)) :=
      preservesColimitsOfShape_discrete_restrictedDerivedPushforward j
    exact isPerfect_of_isCompactObject_spec _ ((restrictedDerivedRestrict j).obj K)
      (isCompactObject_map_of_adjunction (restrictedDerivedRestrictAdjunction j) hK)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0A9A]** (Rouquier, Theorem 6.8). Let `X` be a quasi-compact and
quasi-separated scheme and let `T ⊆ X` be a closed subset such that `X ∖ T` is quasi-compact.
Then `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` is generated by a single perfect object: there is a perfect object `P` of
`D(𝒪_X)` lying in `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` such that every object `E` of `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` with
`Hom(P[n], E) = 0` for all `n ∈ ℤ` is zero.

Generation is [Stacks, Tag 09SJ] for `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)`, written out; morphisms of the full
subcategory are morphisms of `D(𝒪_X)`. The generator is the compact one of
`Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.hasCompactSupportedGenerators`, built by the induction of the
source, and it is perfect by
`Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration.isPerfect_of_isCompactObject`. -/
@[stacks 0A9A]
theorem exists_isPerfect_quasiCoherentSupported_isWeakGenerator_of_qcqs (X : Scheme.{u})
    [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] (T : Set X) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : IsCompact Tᶜ) :
    ∃ P : DerivedCategory X.Modules,
      AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.IsPerfect (X := X.toRingedSpace) P ∧
        quasiCoherentSupported X T P ∧
        ∀ E : DerivedCategory X.Modules, quasiCoherentSupported X T E →
          (∀ (n : ℤ) (g : P⟦n⟧ ⟶ E), g = 0) → IsZero E := by
  obtain ⟨G, hGc, hGT, hGgen⟩ := hasCompactSupportedGenerators X T hT hTc
  refine ⟨G.obj, isPerfect_of_isCompactObject X G hGc, ⟨G.2, hGT⟩, fun E hE h => ?_⟩
  let E' : Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X := ⟨E, hE.1⟩
  exact (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := X.Modules)
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf)).ι.map_isZero
      (hGgen E' hE.2 ((Stacks.Duality.QcqsGeneration.forall_hom_shift_eq_zero_iff _ G E').2 h))

end Stacks.Duality.SupportedGeneration

end
